From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: VyOS LS1046A <ask20@vyos-ls1046a-build>
Date: Thu, 14 Aug 2026 19:30:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] firewall: enable hw-tc-offload for hardware flowtables (035)

On the NXP LS1046A the DPAA1 netdev (fsl_dpa) advertises NETIF_F_HW_TC
as a toggleable feature that defaults to OFF (board patch
0104a-dpaa-netdev-advertise-hw-tc), and the standard
`set interfaces ethernet eth<n> offload hw-tc-offload` config never
applies the toggle at runtime (the offload `possible` predicate path does
not fire for this netdev).  As a result `set firewall flowtable ...
offload hardware` fails its own verify with:

    Interface "eth3" requires "offload hw-tc-offload"

even though `ethtool -K eth3 hw-tc-offload on` succeeds by hand.

Fix, mirroring the vyos-1x-025 ingress-policer pattern (which already
switches the feature on directly via `ethtool -K` for the same reason):

1. verify_hardware_offload(): only reject when the feature is `fixed`
   off (adapter cannot support it).  A toggleable-but-off state is no
   longer an error because apply() switches it on before the flowtable
   is installed.

2. apply(): for every interface of a `offload hardware` flowtable, run
   `ethtool -K <ifname> hw-tc-offload on` BEFORE `nft --file` installs
   the flowtable (nft rejects `flags offload` flowtables on netdevs
   without NETIF_F_HW_TC).

diff --git a/src/conf_mode/firewall.py b/src/conf_mode/firewall.py
index 32356f6..6d74f78 100644
--- a/src/conf_mode/firewall.py
+++ b/src/conf_mode/firewall.py
@@ -511,8 +511,11 @@ def verify_hardware_offload(ifname):
     if not enabled and fixed:
         raise ConfigError(f'Interface "{ifname}" does not support hardware offload')
 
-    if not enabled:
-        raise ConfigError(f'Interface "{ifname}" requires "offload hw-tc-offload"')
+    # F-192 (LS1046A, 2026-08-14): NETIF_F_HW_TC is toggleable but defaults
+    # OFF on the DPAA1 netdev, and the standard `offload hw-tc-offload`
+    # interface config never applies it at runtime.  apply() switches the
+    # feature on directly (ethtool -K) before the flowtable is installed, so
+    # a toggleable-but-off state here is not an error.
 
 def verify(firewall):
     if 'flowtable' in firewall:
@@ -751,6 +754,18 @@ def parse_firewall_error(output):
     raise ConfigError('\n'.join(error_output))
 
 def apply(firewall):
+    # F-192 (LS1046A, 2026-08-14): the DPAA1 netdev advertises NETIF_F_HW_TC
+    # toggleable but defaults it OFF, and the standard `offload hw-tc-offload`
+    # interface config does not apply it at runtime.  Switch the feature on
+    # for every interface of a hardware flowtable before nft installs it
+    # (nft rejects `flags offload` flowtables on netdevs without
+    # NETIF_F_HW_TC).  Mirrors the vyos-1x-025 ingress-policer pattern.
+    if 'flowtable' in firewall:
+        for flowtable, flowtable_conf in firewall['flowtable'].items():
+            if dict_search_args(flowtable_conf, 'offload') == 'hardware':
+                for ifname in flowtable_conf['interface']:
+                    cmdl(['ethtool', '-K', ifname, 'hw-tc-offload', 'on'])
+
     # Use nft -c option to check current configuration file
     completed_process = subp_run(['nft', '-c', '--file', nftables_conf], capture_output=True)
     install_result = completed_process.returncode
